WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
On the Overground, the Tube and London buses you do not need to buy a paper ticket. You pay as you go: with your contactless bank card, phone or watch, or with an Oyster card topped up with credit.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
When you go in, hold your card to the yellow reader: that is «touching in». When you leave, do it again: that is «touching out», even if the gates are open. If you do not touch out, you may be charged the maximum fare.

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
On the bus you only touch in when you get on.

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:52.900
Use the same card or the same phone to go in and out. If you go in with your phone and out with the physical card, the system thinks they are two incomplete journeys.

5
00:00:52.900 --> 00:01:08.900
Take the card out of your wallet: if you hold several to the reader, it may charge the one you did not want («card clash»). There is a daily and weekly spending cap («capping»): once you reach it, you pay no more. The amounts change every year; check them on the TfL website.

6
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:16.100
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
